general_comments.body:
@josephjaniga the code doesn't take into account that `time` argument can be any moment input, which includes objects. Also it doesn't take into account `formats` being a function.

To implement this properly (if at all) you need to do key-testing to figure out if its moment-input or formats object, and also allow for functions. Also avoid using typeof whenever possible, we have a bunch of utility functions that try to do a better job.

I have to revert this if these are not addressed, otherwise we make the API much worse and edge-casey.

@medinarkhov I meant consistent with the the `basicIsoRegex` and `extendedIsoRegex` in the 2 lines above your new `yearIsoRegex` change: https://github.com/moment/moment/pull/4470/files#diff-e3f27469204308066d413adbf4fe72dfR13

Maybe this:
```js
var yearIsoRegex = /^\s*([+-]\d{6}|\d{4})$/;
```

@ashsearle I'm a bit confused here. In the original issue #3918 Matt pointed out that YYYYMM is actually a shorthand for YYYY-MM, which is not 6 digit years, but year + month, without separator. So I have no idea why 6 digit *years* are being discussed in this fix, when there is no such thing mentioned in the issue.

I can't recall one instance in which a computer spitted out 5-6 digit year and that was correct ... like who is talking about the year 10 000 and beyond... Maybe negative 6 digit years make more sense, but AD... no way.

I'll merge this as is, and then add support for YYYYMM myself, to fix the issue in it's entirety.

